From b5388afaddc1dd3f6c44883fc26ee6a4a95561ac Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 02:12:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/7] B20_R7 H05: sealed statement panels and frozen research
 successors through the custodian

* learning.statement_panels: preregistered spec (closed inclusion rules), custodian-side generation
  from a private seed, screening against research exposure, public sources and everything already
  sealed (partition builder; new exposure route 'sealed'), reference obligation by the variety's
  decider, generation record with every count, INSUFFICIENT_DISTINCT_MATERIAL refusal.
* learning.research_export: equational research frozen as a hash-chained campaign export
  (successor manifests, proof objects, exposure, write-once candidate and baseline descriptors).
* candidates: kind formal-research-successor-v1 (statement + library statements only; E inside the
  OCI sandbox with the pinned prover mounted read-only; strict claim decoder; runc only).
* kernel.receipts: genesis-statement-evaluation-request-v1, statement domains eq_<system>_v1 bound to
  their axioms; descriptor_arms(); receipt v4 reused.
* custodian: register_statements (panel generated at registration, salted commitment, private files,
  sealed statements visible to screen_for_research), evaluate_statements (statement reservations,
  sandboxed arms, Lean replay of every claim as separately accounted verification), recover.
* judge: statement rows (1 only for a CHECKED replay), every claim replayed again from the raw store.
* tests_genesis/test_statement_custody.py (12).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Ee919ZRwjeJ7vDUowbM8dB
